WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.115
Distinctive brand assets trigger your brand in memory:

00:00:03.165 --> 00:00:04.837
visuals like logo and colour,

00:00:04.887 --> 00:00:05.687
sounds,

00:00:05.618 --> 00:00:06.418
characters,

00:00:06.373 --> 00:00:07.915
and words like slogans.

00:00:07.965 --> 00:00:11.602
Oddly, the most used are often the least effective.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:13.818
The ad just says, have a...

00:00:13.868 --> 00:00:14.668
and the whole family finishes it: a break!

00:00:14.659 --> 00:00:19.058
The asset does the work.

00:00:19.767 --> 00:00:21.757
Telstra had no colour it could own,

00:00:21.807 --> 00:00:24.646
so it built handmade stop-motion animals instead.

00:00:24.696 --> 00:00:28.997
Before spending, audit which assets people actually recognise.

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:30.900
Use it like this:

00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:32.009
audit your assets,

00:00:32.059 --> 00:00:33.270
keep the ones that work,

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:35.970
and repeat them until they're yours.
